:: day1_npc_nightgown [nobr]
<h3>The Nightgown</h3>

<p>Someone dressed me while I was unconscious. That thought arrives late — hours after waking, when the initial shock has subsided enough for secondary details to register. Someone removed my clothes — the jerkin, the shirt, the trousers, the smallclothes — from a body that was in the process of being rewritten, and replaced them with this nightgown. White linen. Thin. Fitted to a body that didn't fully exist when it was put on.</p>

<p>The nightgown is Silverveil-made — the fabric has that faint enchanted quality, slightly warmer than it should be, slightly softer than any linen I've ever felt. It has a drawstring at the neckline. Whoever put it on me pulled the drawstring loose, probably because my chest was still changing and a tight neckline would have been painful.</p>

<p>The breast band was not on when I woke. The breasts were loose under the nightgown. Someone made the decision that a breast band was unnecessary for an unconscious woman whose breast tissue was still developing. Someone handled these breasts while I wasn't aware of it — clinically, for medical purposes, as part of post-operative care. But someone touched them. Someone saw them before I did.</p>

<p>The thought is not violating, exactly. Ilara is a healer. The sorceresses are medical professionals. But the intimacy of it — the fact that my new body was known by others before it was known by me — adds to the fundamental off-balance feeling that defines this day.</p>

<p>Where are my old clothes? I look around. Not in the room. Someone removed them. The jerkin with the reinforced shoulders. The boots, broken in perfectly. The sword belt. Gone. Probably folded and stored somewhere, relics of a body that no longer fits them, artifacts of a person who walked into this tower yesterday and didn't walk out.</p>

<<set $d1f_npc_nightgown to true>>

